he missing expressions?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "355c5dfd-d06f-56ef-9c38-8dccf702467e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Lagrange System With Two Constraints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b59bf81-336b-5b77-a5ab-993e5da369cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ and $2z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401393} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2b1eac-ff7d-50ba-8e40-931f60aee6f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401394} {:answer/id #uuid "372a272b-dcaf-5ac5-a75d-2792619b147e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x$ and $2y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401395} {:answer/id #uuid "92eb8681-34a4-5d3f-9b19-cabe81d62073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x$ and $2z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401396} {:answer/id #uuid "eda1895b-7d76-519b-8bab-824851119ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "372a272b-dcaf-5ac5-a75d-2792619b147e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x$ and $2y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401395} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec7c466-5f47-5c18-934e-2ba7c46ca3fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8afa6e7b-08b3-5fd6-b960-921c9d4bc534" :question/math-academy-id "q-162811" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${y}^{2}+z=9$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩=\\lambda ⟨\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\boxed{}\\,,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the maximum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,h(x,y,z)={y}^{2}+z=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=1 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\,2y,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "355c5dfd-d06f-56ef-9c38-8dccf702467e" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Lagrange System With Two Constraints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a26a345-848a-52d6-9cff-309d48842caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z\\,$ and $2x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401400} {:answer/id #uuid "0336a2fb-21ec-5932-b4bf-96df7edcc264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\,$ and $x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401401} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3832c6-972f-5f02-873d-640f27294ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\,$ and $2z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401402} {:answer/id #uuid "f73da70f-25e8-5f76-94d0-6c2f5b70918f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\,$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401403} {:answer/id #uuid "13062583-c8cd-58e7-92bd-33acf71104ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\,$ and $-y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3832c6-972f-5f02-873d-640f27294ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\,$ and $2z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401402} :answer-field/id #uuid "6944c355-576e-5c8e-b344-9b3d5fd644ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a114a88-7824-55e2-8ac4-08f991d5f004" :question/math-academy-id "q-162812" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-x=0$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩=\\lambda ⟨-1,\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\boxed{}\\,⟩ \\\\ y-x=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=y-x=0,\\,h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=0 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
